From e0ddcff67d7a928b2b5038ab8fa04941dda7b1a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briansp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:13:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ggml-cuda: RDNA4 FA band: 64-wide K/V load batches,
 forward K order (bit-exact)

The RDNA4 GQA decode/verify band (flash_attn_ext_f16<256, 256, 4, 8>) staged K
and V in one 128-half2 batch. With native q8_0 K/V it read its cache at
~310 GB/s (half the DRAM rate) and sits at 256 VGPRs with scratch spills.

Give the band its own MMA config row (RDNA4, ncols2 == 8, 256-dim heads) that
loads K and V in two 64-half2 batches: 12-14 % faster on gfx1201 (head 256,
GQA 6, n_q 1..4): kv 51200 380 -> 336 us, kv 98304 685 -> 587 us. The config
lookup now carries ncols2 (host helpers take it explicitly, device helpers
default it to 1) so the prefill kernels keep the existing table unchanged.

The K batches were iterated in reverse for MLA's K->V tile reuse, which would
change the head-dimension accumulation order once K is split. A 256-dim
non-MLA head now iterates them forward, so the band is bit-identical to the
single-batch row; every other 256-dim config loads K in one batch and MLA
keeps the reverse order.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
